Subject: [PATCH 15/15] =?UTF-8?q?Cloud-Dialer:=20visual=20redesign=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20spam-danger=20palette,=20shape=20system,=20elevated?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20cards?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Research-grounded pass (Google Phone Material 3 Expressive, Truecaller spam
color legend, iOS Phone, Material 3 system tokens) applied only where safe
against this appʼs real, locally-editable resources — no blind overrides of
unverified org.fossify:commons AAR resources.

- New spam-danger palette (light+dark): distinct from color_missed_call —
  Truecaller reserves red exclusively for spam, never a lesser state.
- In-call screen: bigger bold caller name (34->40sp), dedicated caller-number
  size, spam chip escalated to a filled pill (icon + all-caps + own danger
  colors), thin red ring around the avatar on suspected-spam calls, bigger
  avatar (172->208dp), in-call action-button grid reshaped from circles to
  squircles (local circle_button_background_ripple.xml, corner-radius
  token) with mic/speaker/hold moved onto it too (adds ripple feedback they
  previously lacked).
- Recents list: rows are now elevated tonal cards (own background/margins),
  bigger circular avatars, bold names; spam rows get a dedicated tonal-red
  card + color (previously reused color_missed_call — conflated missed vs.
  spam). Fixed a real recycling bug: card background is now explicitly
  reset on non-spam bind, not just set on the spam branch.
- Dialpad digits: bold weight for hierarchy against the alpha-0.8 letters.
- Main FAB + in-call buttons share one squircle shape language via a new
  DialerFabShape style.
- Settings: spam section label gets a small tinted warning glyph, visually
  linking it to the new in-call/recents spam treatment.

New assets: ic_warning_vector (standard Material warning glyph — the one
genuinely new icon needed), avatar_ring_frame, three recents-card
drawables. Everything else reshapes/retints existing local files.
